<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2/concepts/100509> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2/concepts/100507> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Y STATION"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "A site, incorporating radio masts, built for high-frequency direction finding of enemy vessels and aircraft based on the interception of radio transmissions. Originally established during the First World War they were again used during the Second World War."@en .

<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2/concepts/100514> a skos:Concept ;
