    skos:scopeNote "Blocks of solid concrete, in the shape of a round bottomed cone usually 2 feet 6 inches across x 2 feet 9 inches high. Buoys were mainly used in road blocks intended to impede enemy movement in the event of invasion."@en .

<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2/concepts/160298> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "Caltrop"@en ;
    skos:broader <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2/concepts/91052> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2> ;
    skos:prefLabel "ANTI TANK CALTROP"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Blocks of concrete with four protruding arms so that, whichever way up the caltrop is placed, one arm will always point upward. Used in imitation of the iron caltrops thrown on the ground to impede cavalry."@en .

<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/eh_tmt2/concepts/160300> a skos:Concept ;
